{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0AFL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\infty$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-definition-dimension-at-point}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{examples-section-Noetherian-infinite-dimension}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b5187ddbf4c79da65c401acec09beac32062506a3d70dacf3e5f1af710851681", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ba6b8fbb59bbb5fb0ae46573b01908cffe1196b07adc57683ed80a4539d4fe5a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can define the dimension of an algebraic stack <MATH_0001>\nat a point <MATH_0002>, using the notion of dimension of an algebraic space\nat a point (Properties of Spaces, Definition\n<REF_0001>).\nIn the following lemma the output may be <MATH_0003> either because\n<MATH_0004> is not quasi-compact or because we run into the\nphenomenon described in Examples, Section\n<REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8f7788017a47d29f8832e9ca2f98910c0946c13faa6403cbb38bcd2f798ee8b", "unit_id": "tag:0AFL:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0AFL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$[U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$u \\in U$", "MATH_0008": "$x$", "MATH_0009": "$e : U \\to R$", "MATH_0010": "$s : R \\to U$", "MATH_0011": "$R_u$", "MATH_0012": "$s : R \\to U$", "MATH_0013": "$u$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\dim_x(\\mathcal{X}) = \\dim_u(U) - \\dim_{e(u)}(R_u) \\in \\mathbf{Z} \\cup \\infty\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$u$", "MATH_0016": "$x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-definition-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-dimension-at-point-well-defined}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d23dd2566335b89872208039e990497a3d3da588ad64f640b509c9a34457d3d7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fd44282fbf30896bbc3b1df4acf03e03459993535c1f93bfc0031d56283e578", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian algebraic stack over a scheme <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a point of <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a presentation\n(Algebraic Stacks, Definition <REF_0001>)\nwhere <MATH_0006> is a scheme. Let <MATH_0007> be a point that maps to <MATH_0008>.\nLet <MATH_0009> be the ``identity'' map and let <MATH_0010> be the\n``source'' map, which is a smooth morphism of algebraic spaces. Let <MATH_0011>\nbe the fiber of <MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013>. The element\n<MATH_0014>\nis independent of the choice of presentation and the point <MATH_0015> over <MATH_0016>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4589117bf33b49af3400fc5928de043506868eb7c9258ddd23a871c26a8cfa4", "unit_id": "tag:0AFM:statement"}
